1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,600
Form emails not arriving?
Test your site in one minute.

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:07,400
In WordPress, open Easy Form Builder,
then Panel and Settings.

3
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:10,700
Choose the Email Settings tab.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,800
Press Check Email Server.
Your site sends one real test email.

5
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:18,400
A minute later, you get
a score out of 100.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,800
Three lines below explain the score:
Sender permission (SPF),

7
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:28,200
Email signature (DKIM) and
Domain protection policy (DMARC).

8
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:33,000
Each line marked Needs setup
is a missing DNS record.

9
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:38,000
Your host or email service gives you
the values to copy.

10
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:42,500
Add them in your DNS panel,
then test again.

11
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,800
Run the check again.
Aim for a score above 80.

12
00:00:48,300 --> 00:00:52,500
Full guides for each record
are linked below.
